</Tag>
<Tag Name="PCV101" TagType="Alias" AliasFor="AnalogPoint[29]" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Filtrate Pressure Control Valve Position]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
</Tags>
<Programs Use="Context">
<Program Use="Context" Name="MainProgram">
<Routines Use="Context">
<Routine Use="Target" Name="PCV101" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[[ (Source - LowScale) * 100 ] / ( HighScale - LowScale)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,3)CPT(PCV101_PID.PV,(MOLD_TFF:I.Data[6]-PCV101_PID.ClosedRawValue)*100/(PCV101_PID.OpenRawValue-PCV101_PID.ClosedRawValue));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[[ (Source - LowScale) * 100 ] / ( HighScale - LowScale)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,0)CPT(PCV101_PID.PV,(MOLD_TFF3:I.Data[6]-PCV101_PID.ClosedRawValue)*100/(PCV101_PID.OpenRawValue-PCV101_PID.ClosedRawValue));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(PCV101_PID.PV,PCV101.CurrentValue)MOV(PCV101_PID.PV,PID15.PV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear all auto mode flags when loop is placed in manual mode.  If the loop is enabled, set the manual set point to the current CV for bumpless transfer.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.Manual)ONS(PID15.ManualOSR)[OTU(PID15.Auto1) ,XIC(PID15.Enable) [MOV(PID15.CV,PID15.SPManual) ,MOV(PID15.CV,PID15.SPManualSave) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear manual mode flag and all other auto mode flags when loop is placed in auto mode 1.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.Auto1)ONS(PID15.Auto1OSR)OTU(PID15.Manual);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy the auto set point to be used based on the mode.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID03.PID.SWM)MOV(PID03_RAMP_OUT,PID15.SPAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the HI and LO limits based on the deadband.  If the process variable is within these limits, set the deadband OK status flag.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CPT(PID15.DBLO,PID15.SPAuto-(PID15.SPAuto*PID15.Deadband/100)) ,CPT(PID15.DBHI,PID15.SPAuto+(PID15.SPAuto*PID15.Deadband/100)) ,LIM(PID15.DBLO,PID15.PV,PID15.DBHI) OTE(PID15.DBOK) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the loop is in manual mode, save the current PV as the saved auto set point.  This will cause the output to ramp to the auto set point when switched from manual to auto.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.Manual)MOV(PID15.PV,PID15.SPAutoSave);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the ramping function is disabled and the loop is in manual, copy the manual set point to the CV.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(PID15.RampEnable)XIC(PID15.Manual)MOV(PID15.SPManual,PID15.PID.SO);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the ramping function is disabled and the loop is in manual, copy the manual set point to the CV.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID03.CV_On_Off)XIO(PID15.Manual)[EQU(PID03_RAMP_OUT,100) MOV(0,PID15.PID.SO) ,EQU(PID03_RAMP_OUT,0) MOV(100,PID15.PID.SO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the loop is disabled, clear the saved set points and the ramping control bits.  This will cause the output to ramp to the setpoint when the loop is enabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(PID15.Enable)[CLR(PID15.SPAutoSave) ,CLR(PID15.SPManualSave) ,MOV(PID15.PID.MINO,PID15.PID.SO) ,OTU(PID15.RampUp) ,OTU(PID15.RampDown) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the loop is enabled and the ramping function is enabled and the loop is in auto mode, compare the auto control set point with the saved value and if NEQ, set the auto one-shot and save the new set point for subsequent comparisons.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.Enable)XIC(PID15.RampEnable)XIO(PID15.Manual)NEQ(PID15.SPAuto,PID15.SPAutoSave)[XIO(PID03.CV_On_Off) OTE(PID15.RampAutoOSR) ,MOV(PID15.SPAuto,PID15.SPAutoSave) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the loop is enabled and the ramping function is enabled and the loop is in manual mode, compare the manual control set point with the saved value and if NEQ, set the manual one-shot and save the new set point for subsequent comparisons.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.Enable)XIC(PID15.RampEnable)XIC(PID15.Manual)NEQ(PID15.SPManual,PID15.SPManualSave)[OTE(PID15.RampManualOSR) ,MOV(PID15.SPManual,PID15.SPManualSave) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Save the current loop CV as the ramp starting point when the ramp function is initialized.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PID15.RampAutoOSR) ,XIC(PID15.RampManualOSR) ,NEQ(PID15.RampRate,PID15.RampRateSave) ][MOV(PID15.CV,PID15.RampStart) ,MOV(PID15.RampRate,PID15.RampRateSave) ,RES(PID15.RampTimer) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[At the start of an auto mode ramp, if the new set point is greater than the current PV, set the ramp up flag and clear the ramp down flag if control is SP-PV or set the ramp down flag and clear the ramp up flag if control is PV-SP.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampAutoOSR)GRT(PID15.SPAuto,PID15.PV)[XIO(PID15.PID.CA) [OTL(PID15.RampUp) ,OTU(PID15.RampDown) ] ,XIC(PID15.PID.CA) [OTL(PID15.RampDown) ,OTU(PID15.RampUp) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[At the start of an auto mode ramp, if the new set point is less than the current PV, clear the ramp up flag and set the ramp down flag if control is SP-PV or clear the ramp down flag and set the ramp up flag if control is PV-SP.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampAutoOSR)LES(PID15.SPAuto,PID15.PV)[XIC(PID15.PID.CA) [OTL(PID15.RampUp) ,OTU(PID15.RampDown) ] ,XIO(PID15.PID.CA) [OTL(PID15.RampDown) ,OTU(PID15.RampUp) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[At the start of a manual mode ramp, if the new set point is greater than the current CV, set the ramp up flag and clear the ramp down flag. If the new set point is less than the current CV, set the ramp down flag and clear the ramp up flag.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampManualOSR)[GRT(PID15.SPManual,PID15.CV) [OTL(PID15.RampUp) ,OTU(PID15.RampDown) ] ,LES(PID15.SPManual,PID15.CV) [OTL(PID15.RampDown) ,OTU(PID15.RampUp) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clamp the ramp slope from 0.5 pct/sec to 100.0 pct/sec.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(PID15.RampRate,PID03.RampRate*0.2+PID03.RampRate)[LES(PID15.RampRate,0.5) MOV(0.5,PID15.RampRate) ,GRT(PID15.RampRate,100) MOV(100,PID15.RampRate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enable the ramp timer if ramping up or down.  The timer is reset when not ramping and when a new ramp is started during a ramp.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PID15.RampUp) ,XIC(PID15.RampDown) ]XIO(PID15.RampAutoOSR)XIO(PID15.RampManualOSR)TON(PID15.RampTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When ramping up in manual mode and the CV is GEQ the manual set point, clear the ramp up flag and set the CV equal to the manual set point.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampUp)XIC(PID15.Manual)GEQ(PID15.PID.SO,PID15.SPManual)[OTU(PID15.RampUp) ,MOV(PID15.SPManual,PID15.PID.SO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When ramping up in auto mode, if the PV is GEQ the auto set point and control is SP-PV or if the PV is LEQ the auto set point and control is PV-SP or if the loop is within deadband or if the CV the max value, clear the ramp up flag.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampUp)XIO(PID15.Manual)[XIO(PID15.PID.CA) GEQ(PID15.PV,PID15.SPAuto) ,XIC(PID15.PID.CA) LEQ(PID15.PV,PID15.SPAuto) ,XIC(PID15.DBOK) ,GEQ(PID15.CV,PID15.PID.MAXCV) ,XIO(PID03.PID.SWM) ]OTU(PID15.RampUp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When ramping up, calculate the loop CV from y=mx+b where m is the configured ramp slope, x is the current timer value and b is the ramp starting point.  The timer value is divided by 1000 to convert the sub-second timer to seconds.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampUp)CPT(PID15.PID.SO,PID15.RampRate*(PID15.RampTimer.ACC/1000)+PID15.RampStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When ramping down in manual mode and the CV is LEQ the manual set point, clear the ramp down flag and set the CV equal to the manual set point.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampDown)XIC(PID15.Manual)LEQ(PID15.PID.SO,PID15.SPManual)[OTU(PID15.RampDown) ,MOV(PID15.SPManual,PID15.PID.SO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When ramping down in auto mode, if the PV is LEQ the auto set point and control is SP-PV or if the PV is GEQ the auto set point and control is PV-SP or if the loop is within deadband or if the CV is LEQ the min value, clear the ramp down flag.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampDown)XIO(PID15.Manual)[XIO(PID15.PID.CA) LEQ(PID15.PV,PID15.SPAuto) ,XIC(PID15.PID.CA) GEQ(PID15.PV,PID15.SPAuto) ,XIC(PID15.DBOK) ,LEQ(PID15.CV,PID15.PID.MINCV) ,XIO(PID03.PID.SWM) ]OTU(PID15.RampDown);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When ramping down, calculate the loop CV from y=-mx+b where m is the configured ramp slope, x is the current timer value and b is the ramp starting point.  The timer value is divided by 1000 to convert the sub-second timer to seconds.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.RampDown)CPT(PID15.PID.SO,-(PID15.RampRate*(PID15.RampTimer.ACC/1000))+PID15.RampStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set the ramping status flag if ramping up or down.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PID15.RampUp) ,XIC(PID15.RampDown) ]OTE(PID15.RampStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Control loop is stable when enabled and within deadband for time delay or in manual and not raming.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.Enable)[XIC(PID15.DBOK) TON(PID15.StableTimer,?,?) ,[XIO(PID15.Manual) XIC(PID15.StableTimer.DN) ,XIC(PID15.Manual) XIO(PID15.RampStatus) ] OTE(PID15.Stable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PID loop is in manual if control mode is manual or output is ramping or loop is disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PID15.Manual) ,XIC(PID15.RampStatus) ,XIO(PID15.Enable) ,XIC(PID03.CV_On_Off) ,XIO(PID03.PID.SWM) ]OTE(PID15.PID.SWM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(PID15.SPAuto,PID15.PID.SP);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PID loop timer.  Reset every 250 msec.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.PIDEnable)XIO(PID15.PIDTimer.DN)TON(PID15.PIDTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LEQ(PID15.PID.SP,8) MOV(0.25,PID15.PID.KI) ,GRT(PID15.PID.SP,8) MOV(0.08,PID15.PID.KI) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Feed Control PID loop.  Execute every 250 msec.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.PIDEnable)GEQ(PID15.PIDTimer.ACC,5)PID(PID15.PID,PID15.PV,PID15.CV,PID15.CV,0,0,0)RES(PID15.PIDTimer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID03.PID.SWM)XIO(Maint)MOV(PID15.CV,PCV101_PID.CV)MOV(PID15.CV,AnalogOutput[4].ScaledValue);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CONTROL VALVE TUNING ROUTINE]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Maint)XIC(PID15.CVTune.Activate)OTE(PID15.CVTune.Enable);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.CVTune.Enable)[ONS(PID15.CVTune.OSR.0) MOV(PID15.CVTune.MinOutput,AnalogOutput[4].ScaledValue) ,TON(PID15.CVTune.MinTimer,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.CVTune.Enable)XIC(PID15.CVTune.MinTimer.DN)[ONS(PID15.CVTune.OSR.1) EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,3) MOV(MOLD_TFF:I.Data[6],PID15.CVTune.ClosedRaw) ,ONS(PID15.CVTune.OSR.2) EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,0) MOV(MOLD_TFF3:I.Data[6],PID15.CVTune.ClosedRaw) ,ONS(PID15.CVTune.OSR.3) MOV(PID15.CVTune.MaxOutput,AnalogOutput[4].ScaledValue) ,TON(PID15.CVTune.MaxTimer,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PID15.CVTune.Enable)XIC(PID15.CVTune.MaxTimer.DN)[ONS(PID15.CVTune.OSR.4) EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,3) MOV(MOLD_TFF:I.Data[6],PID15.CVTune.OpenRaw) ,ONS(PID15.CVTune.OSR.5) EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,0) MOV(MOLD_TFF3:I.Data[6],PID15.CVTune.OpenRaw) ,MOV(PID15.CVTune.ClosedRaw,PCV101_PID.ClosedRawValue) MOV(PID15.CVTune.OpenRaw,PCV101_PID.OpenRawValue) ,OTU(PID15.CVTune.Activate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Maint)OTU(PID15.CVTune.Activate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Map the analog output values to the output hardware.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,3)CPT(MOLD_TFF:O.Data[3],(100-AnalogOutput[4].ScaledValue)*20.47);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Map the analog output values to the output hardware.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(ThisSystem.MoldType,0)CPT(MOLD_TFF3:O.Data[3],(100-AnalogOutput[4].ScaledValue)*20.47);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
